Subject: Instance Foundation Windows PowerShell Parse Probe Quoting Fault

@ [fault_uuid] 81f3fe8d-8e79-4ee8-82cd-ef04d654c1c3
@ [conversation_uuid] 01a0222c-2511-7323-92bf-a95777601273

& [Context]
  + a combined shell probe attempted to parse the new exact-workspace harness with both PowerShell 7 and Windows PowerShell 5.1

& [Fault]
  + the outer PowerShell invocation interpolated the nested `$null` token before `powershell.exe` received it
  + Windows PowerShell therefore reported an invocation-level `=` command fault even though the nested parser subsequently accepted the script
  + a second direct command-shell attempt also stripped nested PowerShell variable tokens and was rejected as evidence

& [Correction]
  + treat the first Windows PowerShell probe as invalid evidence
  + use a literal script file or correctly single-quoted nested command for the independent Windows PowerShell 5.1 parse and execution gate
  + an encoded literal Windows PowerShell command subsequently parsed all three new evidence and workspace scripts successfully

& [Boundary]
  + no repository source or live Eclipse checkout was changed by the failed probe
  + the fault does not weaken the required PowerShell 7 or Windows PowerShell 5.1 gate
